// Phase 4, slice 2, step 3 (#26): the public PR flow routes, against an
// in-memory D1 with the migrations applied and a hand-built set of pull
// requests whose numbers are worked out below. The clock is fixed at
// 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z, so the default 7-day window opens at
// 2026-10-29T12:00:00Z.
suite github.hooks

env {
	DASHBOARD_EXCLUDE = "bynk-lang/sandbox"
}

stub Clock.now() returns Instant.fromEpochMillis(1793880000000)

--- A viewer's request headers: one address, well within the limit.
fn viewer() -> RequestHeaders {
	RequestHeaders.of(["CF-Connecting-IP: 203.0.113.7"])
}

---
`bynk-lang/bynk`, by people, merged in the window:

- #1: opened 4 Nov 10:00, ready 5 Nov 08:00, enqueued 09:30, merged 10:00.
  Ready to merge 7200 s, open to merge 86400 s, queue 1800 s, size 120.
- #2: opened 4 Nov 06:00, ready 11:00, enqueued 11:10, dequeued (CI_FAILURE)
  11:20, enqueued again 11:40, merged 12:00. 3600 s, 21600 s, 1200 s,
  requeued, size 10.
- #3: opened 3 Nov 00:00, ready before the service saw it (no `ready_at`),
  enqueued 09:00 but dequeued (CI_FAILURE) 09:10, then merged around the
  queue at 12:00, so it has no queue time; size unknown. Open to merge
  43200 s.

So 3 merged; ready to merge over 2 [3600, 7200]: p50 3600, p95 7200; open to
merge [21600, 43200, 86400]: p50 43200, p95 86400; queue [1200, 1800]: p50
1200, p95 1800; size [10, 120]: p50 10. #4 closed unmerged (and a bot's #13, which
doesn't count); #5 merged before the window. A bot's #6 merged in an hour; its #7 is open. #8 is a
draft, #9 has been ready since 25 Oct (an enqueue on 1 Nov with no dequeue
seen is too old to mean it is still queued), #10 is in the queue (after a
dequeue GitHub gave no reason for), #12 was dequeued (CI_FAILURE) and is back
to ready, and #14, first ready on 1 Oct, went back to draft and was made ready
again at 11:30 today. #11 is gone. A private repository and an excluded
one have a merged and an open pull request each, and must not appear.
---
